    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense is positioned for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Kyle Tucker** (79.68) and **Andy Pages** (73.64), who both benefit significantly from a favorable matchup against Merrill Kelly. Kelly\u2019s elevated xERA (5.13) provides a soft landing for both hitters, with **Kyle Tucker** maximizing the SP skill advantage (+19%) and **Andy Pages** capitalizing on his promotion to the #2 spot (+8%). **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.22) also emerges as an elite play; his strong platoon advantage against Mahle (+14%) and the premium lineup placement in the four-hole makes him a cornerstone of today\u2019s production. While **Gunnar Henderson** (63.19) faces the toughest test of the day against Nathan Eovaldi, his elite leadoff role and dynamic platoon edge keep him firmly in the \"Strong\" category despite the talent of the opposing arm.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Liam Hicks**, who fell just short of the starting threshold with a score of 39.67. While **Liam Hicks** showed promise against a right-handed matchup, the negative park factor and a tough SP assignment against Logan Gilbert pushed his daily efficiency below our strict 40.0 floor. We are opting for **Nasim Nunez** (63.69) instead, as his matchup against Petty (5.17 xERA) offers a much more favorable environment for speed production, which remains our primary objective in this Roto chase. Elsewhere, we are closely monitoring the lineup stability of **Wade Meckler** (54.75); while he benefits from a +17% SP skill boost, his proximity to the 50-point range makes him our most volatile starter. We are holding **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, and **Luis Lara** in reserve, keeping an eye on their availability for upcoming series as we manage our game caps.",
